From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Treat riscv64 like arm64: no x86 SIMD, portable bswap64

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against TadaoYamaoka/cshogi]

setup.py unconditionally defines HAVE_SSE4, HAVE_SSE42 and HAVE_AVX2 for
the _cshogi extension, and src/common.hpp only #undefs them again for
__arm64__/__aarch64__. On riscv64 they stay defined, so common.hpp pulls
in <immintrin.h>/<smmintrin.h> and bitboard.hpp uses __m128i/_mm_*
intrinsics, and the build fails with
"fatal error: immintrin.h: No such file or directory".

Add __riscv to the same two guards the arm64 port uses: undefine the x86
SIMD macros so Bitboard falls back to its portable u64 p_[2]
implementation, and include endianness.h, which supplies the
bswap64() that common.hpp only defines for MSVC and GNU x86.
---
 src/bitboard.hpp | 2 +-
 src/common.hpp   | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/bitboard.hpp b/src/bitboard.hpp
--- a/src/bitboard.hpp
+++ b/src/bitboard.hpp
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 #include "square.hpp"
 #include "color.hpp"

-#if defined(__arm64__) || defined(__aarch64__)
+#if defined(__arm64__) || defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__riscv)
 #include "endianness.h"
 #endif

diff --git a/src/common.hpp b/src/common.hpp
--- a/src/common.hpp
+++ b/src/common.hpp
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 #ifndef APERY_COMMON_HPP
 #define APERY_COMMON_HPP

-#if defined(__arm64__) || defined(__aarch64__)
+#if defined(__arm64__) || defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__riscv)
 #undef HAVE_SSE2
 #undef HAVE_SSE4
 #undef HAVE_SSE42
--
2.43.0

